From f539082328852fa1288eacdb273d2ea6e1672a54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicola Nicodemo <nicola084@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:01:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-14:
 disable eusb5 repeater

The shared dtsi enables a PTN3222 eUSB2 repeater at 0x43 on I2C 5 next to
the one at 0x4f. On the 14" (NP940XMA) only the 0x4f repeater exists: it
serves usb_2 (the fingerprint reader). The ACPI tables describe no device
at 0x43 and no PHY references this node. Disable it.
---
 .../dts/qcom/x1e80100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-14.dts    | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-14.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-14.dts
index 37c49d421..c04c54927 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-14.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-samsung-galaxy-book4-edge-14.dts
@@ -230,3 +230,11 @@ &left_spkr {
 &right_spkr {
 	sound-name-prefix = "SpkrLeft";
 };
+
+/*
+ * Only the eUSB2 repeater at 0x4f (usb_2, the fingerprint reader) exists on
+ * this model; the firmware describes nothing at 0x43.
+ */
+&eusb5_repeater {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
-- 
